/-!
# The cone associated to a quasi-coherent graded algebra

Let `S` be a scheme and `𝒜` a quasi-coherent graded `𝒪_S`-algebra whose structure map
`𝒪_S ⟶ 𝒜₀` is an isomorphism.  The *cone*, or *affine cone*, associated to `𝒜` is the relative
spectrum `C(𝒜) = Spec_S(𝒜)`.  Its structure morphism `π : C(𝒜) ⟶ S` is affine and its direct
image `π_* 𝒪_{C(𝒜)}` is `𝒜` again, with the homogeneous pieces of `𝒜` sitting inside it: this is
the data of an `AlgebraicGeometry.AbstractCone`, the abstract cones of Tag 062R.

Nothing here assumes that `𝒜` is generated by `𝒜₁` over `𝒪_S`.  The source omits that hypothesis
deliberately, in order to agree with [EGA II, (8.3.1)].

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.GradedConeAlgebra` is the datum the construction consumes: a quasi-coherent
  graded `𝒪_S`-algebra, commutative and concentrated in nonnegative degrees, whose degree-zero
  piece is `𝒪_S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.GradedConeAlgebra.algebraSheaf` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.GradedConeAlgebra.situation` present it as a quasi-coherent sheaf of
  commutative `𝒪_S`-algebras, respectively as a relative-spectrum situation.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.GradedConeAlgebra.cone` is **the cone `C(𝒜) = Spec_S(𝒜)`**, with
  `AlgebraicGeometry.GradedConeAlgebra.projection` its projection to the base.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.GradedConeAlgebra.pushforwardValIso` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.GradedConeAlgebra.directSumToPushforward` identify the module underlying
  the algebra sheaf with the direct image, and compare the objectwise direct sum of the
  homogeneous pieces with it.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.GradedConeAlgebra.ι` is the inclusion of the homogeneous piece of degree `n`
  of `𝒜` into `π_* 𝒪_{C(𝒜)}`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.GradedConeAlgebra.isAffineHom_projection`: **the projection of a cone is
  affine**, the relative spectrum of a quasi-coherent algebra being affine over its base.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.GradedConeAlgebra.directSumIsoPushforward`: **the direct image
  `π_* 𝒪_{C(𝒜)}` is `𝒜`** — its underlying `𝒪_S`-module is the sheafification of the objectwise
  direct sum of the homogeneous pieces of `𝒜`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.GradedConeAlgebra.pushforwardHomogeneousSum_eq`: the finite-support sum of
  homogeneous local sections used by `AbstractCone` is `directSumToPushforward` on sections.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.GradedConeAlgebra.decomposition_locally`: **every local section of
  `π_* 𝒪_{C(𝒜)}` is locally a finite sum of homogeneous sections of `𝒜`**.

## Implementation notes

The sheaf of algebras is `Stacks.RelativeSpec.ungradedAlgebraSheaf`, the sheafification in
`CommRingCat` of the objectwise direct sum of the homogeneous pieces, and not
`Stacks.RelativeSpec.gradedAlgebraSheaf`, which sheafifies in `RingCat` and then lifts.  The
reason is quasi-coherence: it is the former whose quasi-coherence is available
(`Stacks.RelativeSpec.isQuasicoherent_ungradedAlgebraSheaf`), and quasi-coherence is what the
relative spectrum requires.

Quasi-coherence is asked of the sheaf of algebras rather than of the coproduct
`∐ n : ℕ, 𝒜 n` directly.  Stating it with the coproduct would need the `HasColimitsOfShape
(Discrete ℕ)` instance for `𝒪_S`-modules, whose synthesis exceeds the default budget in this
import closure; `Stacks.RelativeSpec.isQuasicoherent_ungradedAlgebraSheaf` is the bridge from
the coproduct form, and `Stacks.RelativeSpec.coprodIsoUnderlyingModule` says that the module in
question is that coproduct.

`pushforwardValIso` is `Stacks.AffineAlgebraEquivalence.pushforwardAlgebraIso`, Tag 01LX(3),
read on underlying modules by `Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.underlyingModuleIso`.  The
module underlying `Stacks.AffineAlgebraEquivalence.pushforwardAlgebra π` is `π_* 𝒪` on the nose,
which is `GradedConeAlgebra.underlyingModule_pushforwardAlgebra_projection`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 062Q](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/062Q)
